WEBVTT

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:04.129
This place was a great choice.

00:00:04.296 --> 00:00:05.756
The food is amazing.

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:07.508
And such generous portions.

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:10.260
If you liked the meal just wait
till you try these after-dinner mints.

00:00:10.385 --> 00:00:13.222
You know, Doug,
most guys are put off by my eye.

00:00:13.388 --> 00:00:15.891
It's nice to finally meet
someone who's open-minded.

00:00:18.477 --> 00:00:19.770
Ew!

00:00:50.342 --> 00:00:52.094
What was wrong with your date last night?

00:00:52.344 --> 00:00:55.806
I don't know. Something I couldn't
quite put my finger on.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.183
Possibly his vile lizard tongue.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.602
- You're too picky.
- Yeah.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.981
If you rule out every guy
with a lizard tongue or a low I.Q.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:06.942
or an explosive, violent temper
of course you're gonna be lonely.

00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:09.403
There's nothing wrong
with having high standards.

00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:11.905
- Now, can we please...
- The female Leela's problem

00:01:11.989 --> 00:01:13.282
is purely medical.

00:01:13.365 --> 00:01:15.617
Soon she will drop her eggs
and they will hatch

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.452
and all will be well.

00:01:17.536 --> 00:01:19.705
You just have to give guys a chance.

00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:21.748
Sometimes you meet a guy
and think he's a pig

00:01:21.832 --> 00:01:25.127
but then later on, you realize
he actually has a really good body.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.921
Thank you all for the inspiring advice.

00:01:28.005 --> 00:01:30.382
But I'm perfectly happy with my life
the way it is.

00:01:30.465 --> 00:01:32.426
That sounds like a cry for help.

00:01:32.593 --> 00:01:34.178
Let's all take her out tonight.

00:01:34.261 --> 00:01:36.221
There's lots of great places
to meet people.

00:01:36.346 --> 00:01:39.141
- The Federal Sex Bureau.
- A saucy puppet show.

00:01:39.224 --> 00:01:41.435
The rotting carcass of a whale.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.270
Mmm... I'll pick.

00:01:50.277 --> 00:01:53.572
Oh, wow, it's totally retro.

00:01:53.739 --> 00:01:55.657
Why's everyone wearing those rings?

00:01:55.741 --> 00:01:58.285
Guh. Because nobody wears them anymore.

00:01:58.368 --> 00:01:59.745
Rings are stupid.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:01.205
I think they look cool.

00:02:01.288 --> 00:02:03.207
Shh! don't let anyone hear you say that.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:05.709
Hey, did that lad just say rings are cool?

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:08.337
- Nope. He said they're stupid.
- Cool!

00:02:10.506 --> 00:02:12.758
So what do you think of that guy
by the bar?

00:02:12.841 --> 00:02:14.384
I don't know. Maybe.

00:02:14.468 --> 00:02:15.844
Forget it. He's gay.

00:02:15.928 --> 00:02:17.679
What? How can you tell?

00:02:17.846 --> 00:02:19.306
I just know these things.

00:02:19.431 --> 00:02:21.391
I've got what they call "gaydar."

00:02:21.475 --> 00:02:23.143
There's no such thing.

00:02:23.227 --> 00:02:24.353
No?

00:02:28.398 --> 00:02:31.318
Okay... I got a lock on him.

00:02:31.527 --> 00:02:33.153
Yup. He's gay.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.322
- Are you sure?
- Definitely.

00:02:35.405 --> 00:02:38.492
Unless I'm getting interference
from a gay weather balloon.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.702
You're from the 20th century?

00:02:40.786 --> 00:02:43.705
That's incredible.
I'm from the 21st century.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.375
No way. We've got so much in common.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:47.751
We sure do.

00:02:47.835 --> 00:02:50.379
Remember when those cyborgs
enslaved humanity?

00:02:50.462 --> 00:02:52.130
Uh... Yeah.

00:02:52.214 --> 00:02:53.257
That rings a bell.

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:55.634
This is Bolt Rollins.

00:02:55.717 --> 00:02:59.763
Bolt is a hyper-sled racer
with ten wins on the pro circuit.

00:02:59.847 --> 00:03:01.515
Hello, beautiful.

00:03:01.682 --> 00:03:04.935
I think she means
ten wins on the gay circuit.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.395
I wish.

00:03:06.478 --> 00:03:08.105
Those cats can really fly.

00:03:24.997 --> 00:03:29.168
This is M-5438, an entity of pure energy.

00:03:29.418 --> 00:03:32.754
That's great. Really, but he's just not
what I'm looking for.

00:03:32.838 --> 00:03:34.339
I understand.

00:03:34.423 --> 00:03:37.301
One day you will evolve
beyond your physical body

00:03:37.384 --> 00:03:40.679
and on that day
I hope you will pick up the phone.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.015
You're impossible.

00:03:43.098 --> 00:03:44.933
It's just as well.

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:49.438
I think he comes from a dimension
that's big on musical theater.

00:03:56.862 --> 00:03:58.739
Psst. I need the apartment tonight.

00:03:58.822 --> 00:04:00.532
Go see a saucy puppet show.

00:04:00.699 --> 00:04:02.159
Can do!

00:04:05.621 --> 00:04:09.041
My, my, my, what's
a beautiful lady like you...

00:04:09.166 --> 00:04:10.375
Oh! Wha... Wah!

00:04:10.459 --> 00:04:12.461
I'm sorry, I thought you had two eyes.

00:04:14.213 --> 00:04:15.589
So, Leela,

00:04:15.672 --> 00:04:18.884
you must've had your pick of the litter
last night at closing time.

00:04:18.967 --> 00:04:22.262
Could you guys please
stop talking about my personal life?

00:04:22.346 --> 00:04:25.807
Yes. Let's all talk about
Leela's personal life later.

00:04:25.891 --> 00:04:28.310
But right now,
we have business to attend to.

00:04:28.393 --> 00:04:30.062
- A delivery?
- No.

00:04:30.145 --> 00:04:32.439
A tax-deductible mission of charity.

00:04:33.941 --> 00:04:35.609
This is Vergon 6.

00:04:35.692 --> 00:04:38.362
- This is Vergon 6.
- Buh.

00:04:38.695 --> 00:04:40.864
It's a sunny little doomed planet

00:04:40.948 --> 00:04:44.409
inhabited by a number
of frisky little doomed animals.

00:04:44.493 --> 00:04:46.036
- Animals?
- That's right.

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:49.039
Animals in desperate need of rescue.

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:51.124
You see, Vergon 6 was once filled

00:04:51.208 --> 00:04:54.419
with the super-dense substance
known as dark matter

00:04:54.503 --> 00:04:58.757
each pound of which
weighs over 10,000 pounds.

00:04:58.924 --> 00:05:01.218
Wait. What about the animals?

00:05:01.343 --> 00:05:05.013
Well, dark matter is extremely
valuable as starship fuel.

00:05:05.222 --> 00:05:09.101
That's why it was all mined out
leaving the planet completely hollow.

00:05:09.268 --> 00:05:11.270
Yes, but what about the animals?

00:05:11.895 --> 00:05:13.564
- The what?
- The animals.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:15.440
I didn't say anything about animals.

00:05:15.774 --> 00:05:18.944
Now, it seems the planet
will collapse within three days.

00:05:19.027 --> 00:05:21.613
Incidentally this will kill
all the animals.

00:05:21.989 --> 00:05:24.199
So we have to bring back
two of each kind...

00:05:24.283 --> 00:05:26.577
- Just like Noah's ark.
- Why two?

00:05:27.786 --> 00:05:30.122
Oh.

00:05:34.042 --> 00:05:37.129
I bet you, Leela's holding out
for a nice guy with one eye.

00:05:37.379 --> 00:05:38.630
That'll take forever.

00:05:38.755 --> 00:05:39.756
What she ought to do

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:42.676
is find a nice guy with two eyes
and poke one out.

00:05:42.885 --> 00:05:44.845
Yeah. That'd be a time-saver.

00:05:44.928 --> 00:05:46.221
Do you mind?

00:05:46.388 --> 00:05:48.849
Here you go.
You can use this as an eye poker.

00:05:48.932 --> 00:05:52.019
Thank you, but I don't care
how many eyes a man has.

00:05:52.186 --> 00:05:53.604
As long as it's less than five.

00:05:53.896 --> 00:05:57.149
All I'm looking for is a guy
who's adventurous, self-confident,

00:05:57.649 --> 00:05:59.026
maybe a snappy dresser.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:02.863
These new uniforms
are pretty snappy, eh, first officer?

00:06:03.197 --> 00:06:04.907
I suppose, Captain.

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:07.743
I'm not as big a fan of velour as you are.

00:06:07.993 --> 00:06:10.954
Now, what do you want to do
about that unidentified ship?

00:06:11.038 --> 00:06:12.039
Destroy them.

00:06:13.123 --> 00:06:14.958
Mmm...

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:17.336
That's got a nice feel to it.

00:06:20.547 --> 00:06:23.967
Captain's journal. Stardate 3000.3.

00:06:24.218 --> 00:06:26.094
Who are you talking to, sir?

00:06:26.345 --> 00:06:28.180
You. Aren't you getting this?

00:06:30.599 --> 00:06:33.685
We've detected a vessel
attempting to break the security cordon

00:06:33.769 --> 00:06:35.646
around Vergon 6.

00:06:35.854 --> 00:06:38.774
I'm anticipating
an all-out tactical dogfight

00:06:38.857 --> 00:06:40.484
followed by a light dinner.

00:06:41.151 --> 00:06:44.404
Ravioli, ham, sundae bar.

00:06:44.571 --> 00:06:45.572
Hey, look.

00:06:45.781 --> 00:06:47.449
That's Zapp Brannigan's ship.

00:06:47.533 --> 00:06:49.826
Wow. The Zapp Brannigan?

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:50.994
Uh-huh.

00:06:51.078 --> 00:06:52.704
Who's the Zapp Brannigan?

00:06:52.913 --> 00:06:55.165
Shall I fire on them now, sir?

00:06:55.332 --> 00:06:56.416
Not yet, Kif.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:07:00.295
In the game of chess you can never
let your adversary see your pieces.

00:07:00.462 --> 00:07:02.714
What?

00:07:02.798 --> 00:07:05.259
They say Zapp Brannigan
single-handedly saved

00:07:05.342 --> 00:07:08.679
the Octillian system from
a horde of rampaging killbots.

00:07:08.846 --> 00:07:12.391
- Wow.
- A grim day for robotkind.

00:07:12.808 --> 00:07:15.143
But we can always build more killbots.

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:19.147
He's the most decorated captain
in the whole Democratic Order of Planets.

00:07:19.356 --> 00:07:21.567
Leela's got a boyfriend.

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:23.819
No, I don't, but I think
we ought to meet with him

00:07:23.902 --> 00:07:26.029
and see if he'll help us
rescue those animals.

00:07:26.154 --> 00:07:29.658
Well, just in case you guys hit it off
you'll want to take this with you.

00:07:32.744 --> 00:07:34.538
Sir, they're headed straight for us.

00:07:34.621 --> 00:07:36.039
A well-calculated move.

00:07:36.123 --> 00:07:38.000
Straight out of Sun Tzu's classic text,

00:07:38.083 --> 00:07:39.251
The Art of War.

00:07:39.334 --> 00:07:40.711
Or my own masterwork,

00:07:40.794 --> 00:07:43.172
Zapp Brannigan's Big Book of War.

00:07:43.338 --> 00:07:45.716
But the one thing
their captain doesn't realize

00:07:45.799 --> 00:07:46.925
and never will is...

00:07:47.092 --> 00:07:49.469
Sir, they've docked with us
and have come aboard.

00:07:49.553 --> 00:07:51.597
Then I've risked all and lost.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:53.390
Kif, old man, I'll be in the escape pod.

00:07:53.557 --> 00:07:55.767
If that wicker chair I like
survives the slaughter

00:07:55.851 --> 00:07:57.686
have it sent to my P.O. box.

00:08:02.608 --> 00:08:03.859
Hello, I'm Leela,

00:08:03.942 --> 00:08:06.236
Captain of the Planet Express
delivery ship.

00:08:06.403 --> 00:08:08.572
We've come aboard
to plead for your assistance.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.366
- Well, if there's anything...
- I'm in command here.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:12.659
Zapp Brannigan.

00:08:12.743 --> 00:08:15.579
Has my fame preceded me,
or was I too quick for it?

00:08:15.704 --> 00:08:17.539
Oh, not at all.

00:08:17.706 --> 00:08:19.041
I'm just so, uh...

00:08:19.124 --> 00:08:20.792
Really thrilled to meet you.

00:08:21.001 --> 00:08:23.420
You're an impressive piece of captain.

00:08:23.545 --> 00:08:24.963
Beautiful and deadly.

00:08:25.047 --> 00:08:26.590
A potent combination.

00:08:26.715 --> 00:08:29.051
- You don't mean that.
- But I do.

00:08:29.218 --> 00:08:31.303
I doubt I've seen more than
three or four captains

00:08:31.386 --> 00:08:34.556
sexier than you,
and only one who was deadlier.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:36.600
I heard one time,
you single-handedly defeated

00:08:36.683 --> 00:08:40.354
a horde of rampaging somethings
in the something something system.

00:08:40.437 --> 00:08:42.314
The killbots? A trifle.

00:08:42.439 --> 00:08:44.483
It was simply a matter
of outsmarting them.

00:08:44.733 --> 00:08:46.777
Wow, I never would have thought of that.

00:08:46.944 --> 00:08:49.404
You see, killbots have
a preset kill limit.

00:08:49.488 --> 00:08:50.489
Knowing their weakness

00:08:50.572 --> 00:08:53.408
I sent wave after wave
of my own men at them

00:08:53.492 --> 00:08:55.577
until they reached their limit
and shut down.

00:08:55.786 --> 00:08:58.205
Kif, show them the medal I won.

00:09:01.583 --> 00:09:02.668
More, please.

00:09:03.043 --> 00:09:04.336
A little more.

00:09:04.711 --> 00:09:05.838
More.

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.381
Keep going.

00:09:07.464 --> 00:09:10.175
Captain Brannigan, we really need
to talk to you about our mission.

00:09:10.467 --> 00:09:11.802
Whatever it is, I'm willing to put

00:09:11.885 --> 00:09:14.471
wave after wave of men at your disposal.

00:09:14.596 --> 00:09:15.722
Right, men?

00:09:16.265 --> 00:09:17.391
You suck!

00:09:17.683 --> 00:09:20.978
We're hoping to save the animals
of Vergon 6 from extinction.

00:09:21.061 --> 00:09:22.938
- And if you could just...
- Vergon 6?

00:09:23.021 --> 00:09:24.314
This light dinner is over.

00:09:24.398 --> 00:09:25.691
Wait. What's wrong?

00:09:25.774 --> 00:09:27.734
The Democratic Order of Planets prohibits

00:09:27.818 --> 00:09:30.153
interfering with undeveloped worlds.

00:09:30.237 --> 00:09:33.365
It's a little rule known
as "Brannigan's Law."

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:35.325
But people already interfered.

00:09:35.492 --> 00:09:38.036
That planet was mined completely hollow.

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:41.081
Yes, by a Democratic Order
of Planets mining crew.

00:09:41.206 --> 00:09:43.458
Oh. This doesn't make any sense.

00:09:43.709 --> 00:09:46.128
I don't pretend
to understand Brannigan's Law.

00:09:46.211 --> 00:09:47.588
I merely enforce it.

00:09:47.671 --> 00:09:50.299
Fine. We'll save the animals
without your help.

00:09:50.507 --> 00:09:51.925
I'm afraid I can't allow that.

00:09:52.217 --> 00:09:53.302
Guards!

00:09:54.469 --> 00:09:55.596
Wha... What just happened?

00:09:55.679 --> 00:09:57.389
He's throwing us in prison.

00:09:57.514 --> 00:09:58.891
Ah, dang.

00:09:59.141 --> 00:10:00.475
Can I get this wrapped up?

00:10:02.811 --> 00:10:04.688
Ow!

00:10:05.814 --> 00:10:08.817
I might have liked Zapp Brannigan
if he weren't a pompous dimwit

00:10:08.901 --> 00:10:10.235
who threw me in prison.

00:10:10.319 --> 00:10:12.070
You really are too picky.

00:10:12.279 --> 00:10:14.615
Kif, follow me up to the observation deck.

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:16.867
I've got some musing to do.

00:10:19.244 --> 00:10:20.579
Oh, geez.

00:10:22.247 --> 00:10:25.000
I'm facing a formidable
female adversary, Kif.

00:10:25.083 --> 00:10:28.462
- Suggestions?
- I fail to see any problem, sir.

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:31.757
You already imprisoned her
under directive B10.81.

00:10:32.257 --> 00:10:33.884
You mean Brannigan's Law?

00:10:34.718 --> 00:10:36.303
Right. That law.

00:10:36.595 --> 00:10:37.763
Which one?

00:10:38.013 --> 00:10:39.890
Brannigan's Law.

00:10:40.224 --> 00:10:42.518
Kif, you're my best and most loyal friend

00:10:42.601 --> 00:10:44.520
but you've earned my contempt once again.

00:10:44.603 --> 00:10:45.812
As my protégé, you should know

00:10:45.896 --> 00:10:48.857
that the only way to deal
with a female adversary

00:10:48.941 --> 00:10:50.400
is to seduce her.

00:10:50.484 --> 00:10:51.693
Oh.

00:10:51.944 --> 00:10:54.071
This time we are sure
she's a woman, right?

00:10:54.196 --> 00:10:55.489
Yes.

00:10:55.572 --> 00:10:57.824
Good. Invite her to my quarters.

00:10:57.908 --> 00:11:00.869
Oh, and have the boy
lay out my formal shorts.

00:11:01.036 --> 00:11:02.246
The boy, sir?

00:11:02.621 --> 00:11:04.998
You. You lay out my formal shorts.

00:11:07.042 --> 00:11:10.087
The jackass wants
to see you in his quarters.

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:14.132
Good. This will be my chance
to reason with him captain to captain.

00:11:14.216 --> 00:11:16.677
And he wants you to wear this.

00:11:19.096 --> 00:11:21.014
Come and get it.

00:11:22.182 --> 00:11:25.310
Mmm. Welcome to my humble chamber

00:11:25.394 --> 00:11:28.188
or as I call it The Love-Nasium.

00:11:29.189 --> 00:11:30.816
Cham-pag-en?

00:11:30.941 --> 00:11:33.777
I didn't realize
you were such a coin-a-sewer.

00:11:33.902 --> 00:11:36.238
Well, I have studied abroad...

00:11:36.321 --> 00:11:38.031
Or two.

00:11:40.909 --> 00:11:41.910
- Captain...
- Uh-huh?

00:11:42.035 --> 00:11:43.954
If we could speak seriously for a moment.

00:11:44.079 --> 00:11:45.414
- Uh-huh.
- I'd like you to reconsider

00:11:45.497 --> 00:11:47.332
letting us rescue those animals.

00:11:47.457 --> 00:11:48.625
Mm-hmm.

00:11:56.008 --> 00:11:57.926
I like your style.

00:11:58.051 --> 00:11:59.386
I find it very...

00:11:59.928 --> 00:12:01.221
erotic.

00:12:01.388 --> 00:12:03.140
- What?
- Erotic!

00:12:03.557 --> 00:12:06.727
Erotic! Erotic! Erotic!

00:12:09.146 --> 00:12:10.772
We can definitely escape, Bender.

00:12:10.856 --> 00:12:13.358
All you have to do
is bend the hatch off this steam pipe.

00:12:13.442 --> 00:12:14.902
Hey, yeah.

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:21.450
No good. It's full of steam.

00:12:22.409 --> 00:12:25.454
You look like a woman
who enjoys the finer things.

00:12:25.704 --> 00:12:28.790
Come over here
and feel my velour bedspread.

00:12:29.249 --> 00:12:30.667
I'm not really in the mood.

00:12:30.834 --> 00:12:32.920
Leela, it's real velour.

00:12:33.045 --> 00:12:34.922
Just let yourself go.

00:12:36.298 --> 00:12:38.675
Can I please just go back to prison?

00:12:38.967 --> 00:12:42.763
You'd rather sit in prison
than spend one evening with the Zapper?

00:12:42.971 --> 00:12:44.431
Much rather.

00:12:47.684 --> 00:12:48.894
What are you doing?

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:51.897
Oh, God, I'm pathetic.

00:12:53.106 --> 00:12:54.274
Sorry.

00:12:54.358 --> 00:12:55.484
Just go.

00:12:56.276 --> 00:12:58.237
You want the rest of the cham-pag-en?

00:12:58.362 --> 00:13:01.365
No. And it's pronounced "champagne."

00:13:01.615 --> 00:13:03.534
Oh, God, no!

00:13:04.785 --> 00:13:06.036
It's not a big deal.

00:13:06.578 --> 00:13:07.913
I get so lonely.

00:13:07.996 --> 00:13:11.375
I just thought you,
a fellow captain, would understand.

00:13:11.542 --> 00:13:12.709
